# AutoOps Platform — Cursor Rules

## Repository Layout
This is a pnpm monorepo managed with Turborepo.

```
apps/api          Node.js/Express API  (TypeScript strict)
apps/dashboard    Next.js dashboard    (TypeScript strict)
apps/worker       Background worker    (TypeScript strict)
packages/shared   Shared types/utils   (TypeScript strict)
infra/docker      Docker & Jenkins configs
infra/helm        Helm charts
infra/k8s         Raw Kubernetes manifests
infra/monitoring  Prometheus / Grafana configs
infra/terraform   Terraform infrastructure-as-code
```

## TypeScript
- Always use `strict: true` — no exceptions.
- Prefer `unknown` over `any`; if `any` is unavoidable add a `// eslint-disable` comment explaining why.
- Use explicit return types on exported functions.
- Do not use barrel re-exports that create circular dependencies.

## Code Style
- Single quotes for strings in TypeScript/JavaScript.
- No semicolons in new code (unless enforced by formatter config).
- Trailing commas in multi-line structures.
- Max line length: 100 characters.
- File names: `kebab-case.ts` for modules, `PascalCase.tsx` for React components.

## Imports
- Use absolute workspace package imports (`@autoops/shared`) rather than deep relative paths.
- Group imports: Node built-ins → external packages → internal workspace → relative.

## Infrastructure
- Never hard-code secrets — use environment variables or Kubernetes Secrets.
- All Kubernetes manifests must include resource requests and limits.
- Helm values overrides go in `values-dev.yaml` / `values-prod.yaml`.
- Terraform resources must have meaningful `Name` tags.

## Testing
- Unit tests live next to their source in `test/` subdirectory of each app.
- Smoke tests live in `scripts/smoke-test.ts` of each app.
- Tests use the built-in `node:test` runner — do not add Jest unless explicitly required.

## Docker
- Use multi-stage builds: `builder` → production.
- Never run as root inside containers; use `USER 1000:1000`.
- Always include a `HEALTHCHECK` instruction.
- Build context is the repo root (`docker build -f apps/<name>/Dockerfile .`).

## CI/CD
- Jenkins handles CI: build → test → image push.
- ArgoCD handles CD: GitOps sync from `infra/helm/devops-chart`.
- Do not modify `infra/helm/devops-chart` paths without updating `argocd-devops-app.yaml`.

## Dependency Policy
- Avoid adding dependencies that duplicate what Node.js stdlib provides.
- Pin major versions in `package.json` using `^` caret ranges.
- Run `pnpm audit` before adding any new package.
